{
  "duration": 63.824,
  "frames_30fps": 1915,
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "start": 0.06,
      "end": 5.552,
      "text": "A 14-inch drill bit once drained an entire 1,125-acre lake in three hours."
    },
    {
      "id": "setting",
      "start": 5.712,
      "end": 9.961,
      "text": "On the surface, Lake Peigneur in Louisiana looked like a calm, three-foot-deep fishing pond."
    },
    {
      "id": "hidden",
      "start": 10.101,
      "end": 16.893,
      "text": "But directly underneath the mud sat a massive underground salt mine, 1,300 feet deep, with 55 miners working inside."
    },
    {
      "id": "fail1",
      "start": 17.053,
      "end": 21.36,
      "text": "On November 20, 1980, an oil rig on the lake drilled straight down."
    },
    {
      "id": "fail2",
      "start": 21.48,
      "end": 24.998,
      "text": "At 1,228 feet, the 14-inch bit got stuck."
    },
    {
      "id": "fail3",
      "start": 25.138,
      "end": 29.955,
      "text": "Two and a half hours later, the rig started to tilt. It had punched straight through the ceiling of the salt mine."
    },
    {
      "id": "analogy",
      "start": 30.135,
      "end": 38.028,
      "text": "Now, fresh water dissolves salt. So every gallon pouring through that tiny hole ate away the walls, turning a 14-inch puncture into a half-mile-wide whirlpool."
    },
    {
      "id": "swallow",
      "start": 38.168,
      "end": 44.252,
      "text": "It pulled the plug on the whole lake, swallowing the oil rig, 11 barges, a tugboat, and 65 acres of land."
    },
    {
      "id": "climax",
      "start": 44.412,
      "end": 53.804,
      "text": "The suction was so strong it reversed a 12-mile canal, pulling the Gulf of Mexico backward into a 164-foot waterfall, while 400-foot geysers blasted out of the mine shafts."
    },
    {
      "id": "escape",
      "start": 53.984,
      "end": 59.405,
      "text": "Somehow, every single person escaped. All 55 miners rode one elevator out just in time."
    },
    {
      "id": "twist",
      "start": 59.545,
      "end": 63.574,
      "text": "And days later, nine of the eleven sunken barges popped right back up like corks."
    }
  ],
